From: postmarketOS chopin bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: publish exclusive fences for native JM external BOs

JM already conservatively orders every submitted BO access as exclusive, but
passes imported dma-bufs to kbase with the shared/read-only access bit. Even
with implicit kernel fences enabled, that publishes only shared reader fences,
which other readers and scanout need not wait for.

Match the existing JM access model when submitting external resources. This
publishes producer write fences without adding CPU waits or changing CSF.

--- a/src/panfrost/base/pan_vX_base.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/base/pan_vX_base.c
@@ -86 +86,2 @@
 #include "old/mali-props.h"
+#define BASE_EXT_RES_ACCESS_EXCLUSIVE MALI_EXT_RES_ACCESS_EXCLUSIVE
@@ -1171,8 +1171,11 @@
                 handle_buf[h].last_access[slot] = nr;
                 ++handle_buf[h].use_count;
 
+                /* JM tracks all BO accesses conservatively as exclusive;
+                 * external readers must see a matching producer fence. */
                 if (handle_buf[h].fd != -1)
-                        util_dynarray_append(&extres, base_va, handle_buf[h].va);
+                        util_dynarray_append(&extres, base_va,
+                                             handle_buf[h].va | BASE_EXT_RES_ACCESS_EXCLUSIVE);
         }
 
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&k->handle_lock);
